INT. PUDDING LANE BAKERY - NIGHT - 1666

A low-beamed oven room. Flour in the air. Trays of unbaked loaves. A hearth glowing orange.

Six people sit around a long table, sharing a late supper of bread and cheese by one candle.

MASTER THOMAS FARRIER-WELLS, 50s, baker, at the head. His wife, MISTRESS GWENLLIAN FARRIER-WELLS, 40s. Their journeyman, HOBB PETTIGREW, 20s. The maid, JOAN MACKENZIE-AJAYI, teens. A traveling cloth merchant, ABRAHAM BENVENISTE, 60s. And a young STRANGER in a green cloak, hood up.

THOMAS
Eat. There's more in the oven.

GWENLLIAN
There is always more in the oven.

HOBB
(whispering to Joan)
Not if the master keeps counting.

JOAN
(whispering back)
He counts crumbs.

Abraham chuckles. The Stranger says nothing, breaking bread slowly.

ABRAHAM
Friend, you've eaten little.

STRANGER
I'm saving room.

ABRAHAM
For what?

STRANGER
For the fire.

A silence. Thomas sets down his knife.

THOMAS
Sir?

STRANGER
(throwing back the hood)
Forgive me. My name is Silvanus Carew. I serve the Lord Mayor. I came to warn you.

GWENLLIAN
Of what?

SILVANUS
Of this oven.

THOMAS
My oven has stood thirty years.

SILVANUS
My lord says the wind is wrong tonight.

Thomas stares at him. Joan reaches for the poker, smothers the fire.

THOMAS
Hobb, damp the hearth!

SILVANUS ^
Master baker, damp the hearth!

They speak at once, loud, and the silence afterward is a cliff.

HOBB
Master?

THOMAS
Do it.

Hobb leaps to the hearth, dumps a bucket. Steam billows. The room goes grey. Everyone coughs.

When it clears, Gwenllian is clutching Thomas's sleeve. Joan has her hand over her mouth. Abraham has risen.

Silvanus is smiling, sadly, as he lowers his hood.

SILVANUS (CONT'D)
Too late, I fear. The wind has already come.

From beyond the shutters, faint, a bell begins to ring.
